# skybeta-06: give EKF2 margin for this airframe's vision-latency spikes (see ../../DEBUG_TAKEOFF.md).
#
# Measured with the organisers' tools/latency_probe.py on skybeta-06, 2026-11-08. The camera chain is
# BIMODAL PER BOOT: a clean boot gives image -> bridge p50 72 ms (driver leg 36 ms, = the organisers'
# bench) with spikes to p95 324 / max 418 ms; a bad boot sits at a constant 206-290 ms (backed-up camera
# queue) and never recovers without a stack restart.
# EKF2 fuses a vision sample of age A only if  A + EKF2_EV_DELAY < max(EKF2_DELAY_MAX, EKF2_EV_DELAY) + 100 ms
# (PX4 RingBuffer::pop_first_older_than 100 ms window). Fleet values 70 / 200 -> anything older than ~235 ms is
# dropped -> no local position -> Position refused -> position failsafe disarms on the ground.
#
# EKF2_EV_DELAY stays at the organisers' measured 70 ms (correct on a clean boot; do NOT raise it to
# "fix" a bad boot -- fusing 290 ms-old data as 70 ms-old is the toilet-bowl failure their docs warn about;
# a bad boot is fixed by restarting the stack until jetson/preflight.sh shows the driver leg < 150 ms).
# EKF2_DELAY_MAX 200 -> 400 widens the buffer so the spikes (up to ~435 ms) are still fused instead of dropped.
#
# Load: QGC -> Vehicle Setup -> Parameters -> Tools -> Load from file -> this file -> reboot the FC.
# Verify in the stack:  ros2 topic echo --once /fmu/out/estimator_status_flags | grep -E "cs_ev_(pos|yaw)"
#                       (both true)  and  /skybeta/state "local_enu" non-null, "nav_state_name" POSCTL
#                       with the RC switch on Position while disarmed.
# Revert: EKF2_DELAY_MAX 200 (fleet value).
#
# Vehicle-Id	Component-Id	Name	Value	Type
1	1	EKF2_DELAY_MAX	400.000000	9
